  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT FRI AUG 7 2026\n\nThe weather through the weekend will continue with the\n\"copy/paste\" pattern, as the region remains sandwiched between\nupper-level features to our west, east, and north. This will\nresult in continued rounds of diurnally driven afternoon showers\nand storms, with nothing more organized in the forecast. By\nMonday, the ridge to our east will begin to weaken, as a deep\ntrough and low pressure moves through New England. This will\nallow the trough to the north to reorient itself, taking a more\nNW to SE shape. While this won't have any immediate effect on our\narea, the ridge to our west will start to become suppressed by\nthe middle of next week. This is where rain chances may slightly\nincrease, as this slight transition would allow for a few\nshortwave disturbances to ride the trough, clipping portions of\nthe state. Unfortunately, confidence here is low, as any slight\nchange in the upper-level flow would result in very different\nresults.\n\nOtherwise, high temperatures will continue to reach the low to\nmid-90s during the afternoon hours, with heat index values\nremaining under critical thresholds for the next seven days.\n\n/44/",
